  {
    question: 'Where is the divorce court in Abu Dhabi?',
    answer:
      "Divorce cases in Abu Dhabi are heard by the Abu Dhabi Judicial Department (ADJD). Muslim cases go to the Personal Status circuit of the Court of First Instance at the main ADJD courts complex in Abu Dhabi city, with branch courts in Al Ain and Al Dhafra for residents of those regions. Non-Muslim foreigners use the separate Abu Dhabi Civil Family Court, also run by ADJD. The Family Guidance Department at ADJD handles reconciliation sessions for Muslim cases before they proceed to hearings.",
